course: dictionary
lesson: 11316
title: Yesterday and the past
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yesterday means on the day before today. If today is Tuesday, yesterday was Monday, and tomorrow will be Wednesday. Days are easy to mix up, so check the calendar when you count back.
explain: Yesterday also tells you about time in a sentence. English uses the past tense for things that have finished, so «I played yesterday» is right, and «I play yesterday» is wrong. When you see yesterday, look for a verb in the past tense.
explain: Yesterday can also mean the past in general. Alice says, «it's no use going back to yesterday, because I was a different person then.» She is not only talking about one day. She means the time before now, when things were different.
fact: Yesterday means on the day before today.
fact: The day before yesterday means two days ago.
fact: Yesterday is an adverb in «I played yesterday», and a noun in «the toys of yesterday».
fact: «Yesterday» tells the reader that events happened in the past, so the verbs change: «I played», not «I play».
fact: Other languages have words for yesterday too: «zuótiān» in Chinese and «hier» in French both mean yesterday.
exercise: If today is Tuesday, what day was yesterday? | Thursday | *Monday | Wednesday
exercise: Which sentence is correct? | I play in the park yesterday | I will played in the park yesterday | I playing in the park yesterday | *I played in the park yesterday
exercise: Mole says he came home in «that old washerwoman-dress» yesterday. What does yesterday show? | That Mole will come home tomorrow | That Mole lives in a kitchen | *That Mole came home on the day before today | That the dress is brand new
test: If today is Friday, what day was the day before yesterday? | Thursday | *Wednesday | Friday | Saturday
test: Choose the correct verb: «I ___ my bike yesterday.» | ride | riding | *rode | will ride
exam: Which word means the day before today? | Today | *Yesterday | Tomorrow | Tonight
